  "notes": "The drunk pocket and the extended chord, and it is not this genre without both. The snare sits LATE — a real displacement of a few milliseconds rather than humanizer noise — the hats swing at 63%, somewhere between straight and triplet, and ghost snares crowd almost every e and a, so the bar leans instead of marching. Only jerk is authored looser. The harmony is where the leaning goes: m7/m9/maj9 stacks with triads down at 6%, open voicings, a real ii–v–i and the 3-6-2-5 chain, and a Dorian i–IV vamp. The topline is a Rhodes-and-voice long arc with a low chord-tone bias, free to land on the 9th, 11th and 13th. No 808 — a fingered electric bass plays its own figure.",
